      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ultimately, the debate over foreign aid is not economic; it is an ethical reckoning. To argue for scaled-back aid is to tacitly endorse a world where human rights are privileges reserved by geography, not universal entitlements. A robust commitment to international support is not an optional policy; it is the bedrock of a humane and modern global society. Let us choose a legacy defined not by what we kept safe, but by what we bravely chose to save.",
